<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only -->
<!--
  Pulsar Seat - WiX v3 fragment merged into the Tauri 2 MSI
  (bundle.windows.wix.fragmentPaths / componentRefs, see ../tauri-bundle.json).
  Adapted from pulsar-split (installer/wix/PulsarSplit.wxs, same author, GPL-3.0); since
  merge step 10 it is the one MSI of both seat kinds (local and remote).

  What it adds to the Tauri product (the manager exe is Tauri's main binary):
    * pulsar-seat-service.exe + ServiceInstall (PulsarSeat, LocalSystem, own process,
      automatic, depends on RpcSs + LSM, SID type unrestricted, restart 5 s / 30 s / 120 s,
      reset after 1 day)                                         spec 90 §11, installer/README.md
    * pulsar-seat-host.exe, pulsar-seat-agent.exe
    * pulsar-seat-credprov.dll (file only; registered by the service, never by the MSI)
    * pulsar-seat-wrds.dll (Remote Desktop protocol provider; file only, registered by the
      service while remote seats use the Pulsar display, removed by `uninstall`)
    * machine Run value PulsarSeatManager = "<dir>\pulsar-seat-manager.exe" - -tray
    * HKLM\SOFTWARE\Pulsar Seat: InstallPath, Version (nothing else)
    * deferred, no-impersonate custom actions on our own binary:
        install   - service description / privileges / SDDL, data dir + ACL, Event Log
                    source (service package) + pre-flight gate, restore point, optional
                    tweaks, signed driver packages (seat-compat::setup)
        rollback  - if anything after `install` fails on a fresh install, reverts the
                    journal (tweaks, drivers) before the files are rolled back
        uninstall - stops seats, reverts every journaled change, removes the LSA
                    secrets, driver packages we published, the Event Log source, the
                    passwordless-seat RDP listener and its firewall block rule (made by
                    the service on Server + RDSH only; installer/README.md "Never")
    * interactive upgrade / repair / removal: a yes / no dialog before running seats are
      stopped (ServiceControl Stop="both"); silent runs (/qn) stop them without asking
    * interactive install: an options page (restore point, fast startup / sleep / crash
      dump tweaks, all off by default) that sets PSRESTOREPOINT / PSTWEAKS; interactive
      removal: a page that asks whether to delete %ProgramData%\Pulsar Seat (REMOVEUSERDATA)
    * builds with signed driver packages: ScheduleReboot, so msiexec /norestart returns 3010
    * remote seat kind (merge step 10, from installer/split/wix/PulsarSplit.wxs):
        - the pinned third-party payload below remote\ (drivers.json, drivers\<id>\,
          stream-server.json, stream-server\: Sunshine per arch), generated as
          ComponentGroup PulsarSeatRemotePayload by installer/scripts/bundle-config.ts;
        - the per-process shim (ComponentGroup PulsarSeatShim): shim\x64\, shim\x86\ in both
          packages, plus shim\arm64\ (native ARM64 module, launcher, shimctl) in the ARM64
          package (parity-arm64 2026-11-17);
        - deferred custom actions `remote-setup install` (fresh install) and
          `remote-setup reconcile` (every install / upgrade / repair) after `install`:
          remote data folders, a leftover PulsarSplit service (stopped and deleted),
          third-party drivers only when PULSARDRIVERS names them (default on a fresh
          install: none), passive mode beside the reference product;
        - uninstall: the one `uninstall` action replays both journal formats.
    * interactive install: a non-blocking warning when TermService uses a non-default DLL
      (the other warnings are in %ProgramData%\Pulsar Seat\logs\setup.log and shown by
      the manager on its first start)

    * signed driver packages: drivers\<package>\ from the generated fragment
      (installer/scripts/bundle-config.ts, ComponentGroup PulsarSeatDriverPackages; empty
      unless build-installer.ps1 ran with -SignedDrivers)
    * coexistence guard: refuses to install while the reference multi-seat product's
      service keys exist (interop identifiers, spec 90 §11 item 4)
    * architecture guard: the x64 MSI refuses an ARM64 PC and vice versa.

  Public properties (command line, e.g. msiexec /i PulsarSeat.msi /qn PSRESTOREPOINT=1):
    PSRESTOREPOINT=1                   create a System Restore point before system settings change
    PSTWEAKS=fast_startup_off,sleep_off,small_crash_dumps
                                       optional system tweaks (journaled, undone on uninstall);
                                       only a-z, _ and , (launch condition below)
    PULSARDRIVERS=vdd,usbip-win2       remote kind: third-party driver ids from remote\drivers.json
                                       ("none" = none; empty on a repair / upgrade = the choice
                                       saved at the first install; a fresh install without it
                                       installs none, so local-only PCs get no virtual display)
    PULSARCONSENT=usbip-win2           remote kind: ids whose upstream installer may run
    PSWINFEATURES=virtual_machine_platform,hyper_v,windows_sandbox
                                       optional Windows features to turn on (DISM, no restart,
                                       no Windows Update source; journaled, kept at uninstall);
                                       ids from seat-compat features.rs, a-z, _ and , only
    PSIMPORTCERT=1                     import the package's own publisher certificate
                                       (certs\publisher.cer, only in a -PublisherCert build) into
                                       LocalMachine\TrustedPublisher (+ Root when self-signed);
                                       journaled, removed at uninstall; default off
    REMOVEUSERDATA=1                   uninstall also deletes %ProgramData%\Pulsar Seat
                                       (msiexec /x PulsarSeat.msi /qn REMOVEUSERDATA=1); the
                                       updates\ download cache is deleted on every uninstall

  Never: firewall allow rules (local pipe only, spec 90 §11 item 8), Defender exclusions,
  certificates or optional features without the operator's tick (PSIMPORTCERT /
  PSWINFEATURES, unchecked by default), test-signing, DeviceGuard / CI values, Windows Update blocking, files in
  System32, class-wide filter edits. Built with the WiX 3.14 that Tauri's bundler downloads
  (installer/README.md "Build"); never installed on the dev box.

  Build-time input: PULSAR_SEAT_BIN = folder with pulsar-seat-service.exe,
  pulsar-seat-host.exe, pulsar-seat-agent.exe for the architecture being built, plus
  apihelper\<x86|x64[|arm64|arm64ec]>\pulsar-seat-api.dll (the app API helper for every
  app architecture this PC runs; ARM64 folders only in the ARM64 package).
  $(sys.BUILDARCH) is x64 or arm64 (Tauri passes -arch to candle).
  Tauri's candle run does not see the caller's environment variables, so
  installer/scripts/bundle-config.ts (`- -bin <dir>`) writes a copy of this file with
  $(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN) replaced by the payload folder and points the bundle at that copy.
-->
<Wix xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/wix/2006/wi">
  <Fragment>
    <!-- ================================================================ properties -->
    <Property Id="PSRESTOREPOINT" Secure="yes" />
    <Property Id="PSTWEAKS" Secure="yes" />
    <Property Id="REMOVEUSERDATA" Secure="yes" />
    <Property Id="PULSARDRIVERS" Secure="yes" />
    <Property Id="PULSARCONSENT" Secure="yes" />
    <Property Id="PSWINFEATURES" Secure="yes" />
    <Property Id="PSIMPORTCERT" Secure="yes" />

    <!-- Native machine (64-bit registry view; not virtualised for x64 code on ARM64). -->
    <Property Id="PSNATIVEARCH">
      <RegistrySearch Id="PsNativeArch" Root="HKLM" Win64="yes" Type="raw"
                      Key="SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session Manager\Environment"
                      Name="PROCESSOR_ARCHITECTURE" />
    </Property>
<?if $(sys.BUILDARCH) = "arm64" ?>
    <Condition Message="!(loc.PsArchArm64Only)">
      <![CDATA[Installed OR PSNATIVEARCH ~= "ARM64"]]>
    </Condition>
<?else ?>
    <Condition Message="!(loc.PsArchX64Only)">
      <![CDATA[Installed OR PSNATIVEARCH ~= "AMD64"]]>
    </Condition>
<?endif ?>

    <!-- Coexistence: every service key has a `Type` value, so reading it proves the key. -->
    <Property Id="PSREFSEATSERVICE">
      <RegistrySearch Id="PsRefSeatService" Root="HKLM" Win64="yes" Type="raw"
                      Key="SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\MUTESV_SERVICE" Name="Type" />
    </Property>
    <Property Id="PSREFDRIVERSERVICE">
      <RegistrySearch Id="PsRefDriverService" Root="HKLM" Win64="yes" Type="raw"
                      Key="SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\MUTENX_SERVICE" Name="Type" />
    </Property>
    <Condition Message="!(loc.PsCoexistence)">
      <![CDATA[Installed OR (NOT PSREFSEATSERVICE AND NOT PSREFDRIVERSERVICE)]]>
    </Condition>

    <!-- Windows 10 22H2 (19045) or newer. VersionNT is 603 on 10/11, so read the build. -->
    <Property Id="PSOSBUILD">
      <RegistrySearch Id="PsOsBuild" Root="HKLM" Win64="yes" Type="raw"
                      Key="SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion" Name="CurrentBuildNumber" />
    </Property>
    <Condition Message="!(loc.PsOsTooOld)">
      <![CDATA[Installed OR (PSOSBUILD >= "19045" AND PSOSBUILD <> "")]]>
    </Condition>

    <Condition Message="!(loc.PsNeedsAdmin)">
      <![CDATA[Privileged]]>
    </Condition>

    <!-- Public properties reach a SYSTEM command line: allow only what they are for.
         PSTWEAKS: lowercase ids and commas (the service parser refuses anything else
         too); the characters that could split or escape the quoted argument are
         refused here (whitespace is the only argument separator, so without it a stray quote
         cannot start a new argument; MSI condition literals cannot hold a quote). -->
    <!-- Not in CDATA: `&#9;` must be a real tab character in the condition (inside CDATA it
         would be the literal text "&#9;"). The service's own parser
         (seat-compat valid_tweak_list: a-z, _ and , only) stays the real validator. -->
    <Condition Message="!(loc.PsBadTweaks)">Installed OR NOT (PSTWEAKS &gt;&lt; " " OR PSTWEAKS &gt;&lt; "&#9;" OR PSTWEAKS &gt;&lt; "-" OR PSTWEAKS &gt;&lt; "/" OR PSTWEAKS &gt;&lt; "\" OR PSTWEAKS &gt;&lt; "=" OR PSTWEAKS &gt;&lt; "[" OR PSTWEAKS &gt;&lt; "]")</Condition>
    <Condition Message="!(loc.PsBadRestorePoint)">
      <![CDATA[Installed OR NOT PSRESTOREPOINT OR PSRESTOREPOINT = "0" OR PSRESTOREPOINT = "1"]]>
    </Condition>
    <!-- PULSARDRIVERS / PULSARCONSENT reach a SYSTEM command line (quoted argument): ids,
         commas and "-" / "_" only; the same characters as for PSTWEAKS are refused here
         (except "-", which driver ids use; seat-setup's parser refuses unknown ids). -->
    <Condition Message="!(loc.PsBadDrivers)">Installed OR NOT (PULSARDRIVERS &gt;&lt; " " OR PULSARDRIVERS &gt;&lt; "&#9;" OR PULSARDRIVERS &gt;&lt; "/" OR PULSARDRIVERS &gt;&lt; "\" OR PULSARDRIVERS &gt;&lt; "=" OR PULSARDRIVERS &gt;&lt; "[" OR PULSARDRIVERS &gt;&lt; "]")</Condition>
    <Condition Message="!(loc.PsBadConsent)">Installed OR NOT (PULSARCONSENT &gt;&lt; " " OR PULSARCONSENT &gt;&lt; "&#9;" OR PULSARCONSENT &gt;&lt; "/" OR PULSARCONSENT &gt;&lt; "\" OR PULSARCONSENT &gt;&lt; "=" OR PULSARCONSENT &gt;&lt; "[" OR PULSARCONSENT &gt;&lt; "]")</Condition>
    <Condition Message="!(loc.PsBadFeatures)">Installed OR NOT (PSWINFEATURES &gt;&lt; " " OR PSWINFEATURES &gt;&lt; "&#9;" OR PSWINFEATURES &gt;&lt; "-" OR PSWINFEATURES &gt;&lt; "/" OR PSWINFEATURES &gt;&lt; "\" OR PSWINFEATURES &gt;&lt; "=" OR PSWINFEATURES &gt;&lt; "[" OR PSWINFEATURES &gt;&lt; "]")</Condition>
    <Condition Message="!(loc.PsBadImportCert)">
      <![CDATA[Installed OR NOT PSIMPORTCERT OR PSIMPORTCERT = "0" OR PSIMPORTCERT = "1"]]>
    </Condition>
    <Condition Message="!(loc.PsBadRemoveUserData)">
      <![CDATA[NOT REMOVEUSERDATA OR REMOVEUSERDATA = "0" OR REMOVEUSERDATA = "1"]]>
    </Condition>

    <!-- Our service record (upgrade / repair: seats may be running). -->
    <Property Id="PSSERVICEPRESENT">
      <RegistrySearch Id="PsServicePresent" Root="HKLM" Win64="yes" Type="raw"
                      Key="SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\PulsarSeat" Name="Type" />
    </Property>
    <!-- TermService DLL as stored (raw REG_EXPAND_SZ reads come back with a leading "#";
         HYPOTHESIS, the NSIS and Rust checks expand and compare the full path). -->
    <Property Id="PSTERMSRVDLL">
      <RegistrySearch Id="PsTermSrvDll" Root="HKLM" Win64="yes" Type="raw"
                      Key="SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\TermService\Parameters" Name="ServiceDll" />
    </Property>
    <!-- Fast startup state (raw DWORD reads come back as "#<n>"): the options dialog offers
         to turn it off only while it is on (missing value = Windows default, on). -->
    <Property Id="PSHIBERBOOT">
      <RegistrySearch Id="PsHiberboot" Root="HKLM" Win64="yes" Type="raw"
                      Key="SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session Manager\Power" Name="HiberbootEnabled" />
    </Property>
    <!-- Options dialog check boxes (full UI). Pre-set from a PSTWEAKS given on the command
         line; PsOptionsDlg's Next rebuilds PSTWEAKS from them. -->
    <SetProperty Id="PSUI_FASTSTARTUP" Value="1" After="AppSearch" Sequence="ui">
      <![CDATA[PSTWEAKS >< "fast_startup_off"]]>
    </SetProperty>
    <SetProperty Id="PSUI_SLEEP" Value="1" After="AppSearch" Sequence="ui">
      <![CDATA[PSTWEAKS >< "sleep_off"]]>
    </SetProperty>
    <SetProperty Id="PSUI_DUMPS" Value="1" After="AppSearch" Sequence="ui">
      <![CDATA[PSTWEAKS >< "small_crash_dumps"]]>
    </SetProperty>
    <!-- Components dialog check boxes, pre-set from a PSWINFEATURES given on the command line. -->
    <SetProperty Id="PSUI_VMP" Value="1" After="AppSearch" Sequence="ui">
      <![CDATA[PSWINFEATURES >< "virtual_machine_platform"]]>
    </SetProperty>
    <SetProperty Id="PSUI_HYPERV" Value="1" After="AppSearch" Sequence="ui">
      <![CDATA[PSWINFEATURES >< "hyper_v"]]>
    </SetProperty>
    <SetProperty Id="PSUI_SANDBOX" Value="1" After="AppSearch" Sequence="ui">
      <![CDATA[PSWINFEATURES >< "windows_sandbox"]]>
    </SetProperty>

    <!-- ================================================================ files + service -->
    <DirectoryRef Id="INSTALLDIR">
      <Component Id="PulsarSeatServiceComponent" Guid="{87FF2F4E-A397-4BBF-8798-5F5D87F25543}" Win64="yes">
        <File Id="PulsarSeatServiceExe" Name="pulsar-seat-service.exe" KeyPath="yes"
              Source="$(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN)\pulsar-seat-service.exe" />
        <ServiceInstall Id="PulsarSeatServiceInstall"
                        Name="PulsarSeat"
                        DisplayName="!(loc.PsServiceDisplayName)"
                        Description="!(loc.PsServiceDescription)"
                        Type="ownProcess"
                        Start="auto"
                        ErrorControl="normal"
                        Account="LocalSystem"
                        Arguments="--service"
                        Vital="yes">
          <ServiceDependency Id="RpcSs" />
          <ServiceDependency Id="LSM" />
          <ServiceConfig DelayedAutoStart="no" ServiceSid="unrestricted"
                         OnInstall="yes" OnReinstall="yes" />
          <!-- No ServiceConfigFailureActions: Windows Installer opens the service without
               SERVICE_START, so restart actions fail with error 5 (MSI error 1939, seen in
               the ARM64 test VM 2026-11-14). PsSetupInstall (MSI-mode install) sets the
               recovery actions, required privileges and DACL (scm::configure_existing). -->
        </ServiceInstall>
        <!-- Stopping the service stops every seat first (service pre-shutdown path). -->
        <ServiceControl Id="PulsarSeatServiceControl" Name="PulsarSeat"
                        Start="install" Stop="both" Remove="uninstall" Wait="yes" />
      </Component>

      <Component Id="PulsarSeatHostComponent" Guid="{395E4E20-0276-45B2-8E64-DA2E60C770A2}" Win64="yes">
        <File Id="PulsarSeatHostExe" Name="pulsar-seat-host.exe" KeyPath="yes"
              Source="$(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN)\pulsar-seat-host.exe" />
      </Component>
      <Component Id="PulsarSeatAgentComponent" Guid="{ECD52FE0-E7B3-497C-AA8D-9E482CBF301D}" Win64="yes">
        <File Id="PulsarSeatAgentExe" Name="pulsar-seat-agent.exe" KeyPath="yes"
              Source="$(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN)\pulsar-seat-agent.exe" />
      </Component>
      <!-- Credential provider + filter DLL (credprov/, native for this package's arch). The
           file only: no COM or credential-provider registration here. The service registers
           it while the product is enabled under fast user switching and removes it on
           disable; `uninstall` removes our keys too (seat_session::credprov). -->
      <!-- Remote Desktop protocol provider (crates/seat-wrds, native for this package's arch).
           The file only: the service registers its COM class and WinStation listener while
           remote seats use the Pulsar display and removes them otherwise; `uninstall` removes
           our keys too (seat_session::wrds). -->
      <Component Id="PulsarSeatWrdsComponent" Guid="{9C41E7A2-5B3D-4E8F-A1C6-2D7F0B9E4A53}" Win64="yes">
        <File Id="PulsarSeatWrdsDll" Name="pulsar-seat-wrds.dll" KeyPath="yes"
              Source="$(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN)\pulsar-seat-wrds.dll" />
      </Component>
      <Component Id="PulsarSeatCredProvComponent" Guid="{2E8B5D17-9A3C-4F61-B7D4-0C5A8E1F3B26}" Win64="yes">
        <File Id="PulsarSeatCredProvDll" Name="pulsar-seat-credprov.dll" KeyPath="yes"
              Source="$(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN)\pulsar-seat-credprov.dll" />
      </Component>

      <!-- Manager autostart in every interactive session (seat sessions included). -->
      <Component Id="PulsarSeatRunComponent" Guid="{E4955AB3-0A1F-4FFE-8D06-506D72381C31}" Win64="yes">
        <RegistryValue Root="HKLM" Key="SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run"
                       Name="PulsarSeatManager" Type="string"
                       Value="&quot;[INSTALLDIR]pulsar-seat-manager.exe&quot; --tray" KeyPath="yes" />
      </Component>

      <!-- Install facts only (no settings in the registry). -->
      <Component Id="PulsarSeatRegistryComponent" Guid="{7F734EDC-415D-460D-A9EC-D294BDADF8D7}" Win64="yes">
        <RegistryKey Root="HKLM" Key="SOFTWARE\Pulsar Seat" ForceDeleteOnUninstall="yes">
          <RegistryValue Name="InstallPath" Type="string" Value="[INSTALLDIR]" KeyPath="yes" />
          <RegistryValue Name="Version" Type="string" Value="[ProductVersion]" />
        </RegistryKey>
      </Component>

      <!-- Signed driver packages, one folder each (empty today: nothing is signed yet,
           drivers/README.md). The install step stages only Microsoft-signed packages. -->
      <Directory Id="PulsarSeatDriversDir" Name="drivers">
        <Component Id="PulsarSeatDriversDirComponent" Guid="{647E7F87-2BA3-4547-8CCA-04B926F0298E}" Win64="yes"
                   KeyPath="yes">
          <CreateFolder />
        </Component>
      </Directory>

      <!-- App API helper DLL (crates/seat-compat/apihelper), one per app architecture.
           The component ids exist in both packages; the ARM64 / ARM64EC ones are empty
           folders in the x64 package. -->
      <Directory Id="PulsarSeatApiHelperDir" Name="apihelper">
        <Directory Id="PulsarSeatApiHelperX86Dir" Name="x86">
          <Component Id="PulsarSeatApiHelperX86Component" Guid="{3B7C1C1E-6E0B-4C33-9F0E-0E4C4F0C5A11}" Win64="yes">
            <File Id="PulsarSeatApiX86Dll" Name="pulsar-seat-api.dll" KeyPath="yes"
                  Source="$(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN)\apihelper\x86\pulsar-seat-api.dll" />
          </Component>
        </Directory>
        <Directory Id="PulsarSeatApiHelperX64Dir" Name="x64">
          <Component Id="PulsarSeatApiHelperX64Component" Guid="{9F5E2D40-1B0C-4F3A-8C6D-2A7E9B1C3D22}" Win64="yes">
            <File Id="PulsarSeatApiX64Dll" Name="pulsar-seat-api.dll" KeyPath="yes"
                  Source="$(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN)\apihelper\x64\pulsar-seat-api.dll" />
          </Component>
        </Directory>
        <Directory Id="PulsarSeatApiHelperArm64Dir" Name="arm64">
          <Component Id="PulsarSeatApiHelperArm64Component" Guid="{C2A4E6F8-3D5B-4A7C-9E1F-4B6D8A0C2E33}" Win64="yes">
<?if $(sys.BUILDARCH) = "arm64" ?>
            <File Id="PulsarSeatApiArm64Dll" Name="pulsar-seat-api.dll" KeyPath="yes"
                  Source="$(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN)\apihelper\arm64\pulsar-seat-api.dll" />
<?else ?>
            <CreateFolder />
<?endif ?>
          </Component>
        </Directory>
        <Directory Id="PulsarSeatApiHelperArm64ecDir" Name="arm64ec">
          <Component Id="PulsarSeatApiHelperArm64ecComponent" Guid="{5D7F9B1D-4E6A-4C8B-A0D2-6C8E0B2D4F44}" Win64="yes">
<!-- bundle-config.ts -no-arm64ec rewrites the next line to "no": local test builds on a
     toolchain without the arm64ec target (release builds always ship it, ci.yml). -->
<?define PsArm64ec = "yes" ?>
<?if $(sys.BUILDARCH) = "arm64" AND $(var.PsArm64ec) = "yes" ?>
            <File Id="PulsarSeatApiArm64ecDll" Name="pulsar-seat-api.dll" KeyPath="yes"
                  Source="$(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN)\apihelper\arm64ec\pulsar-seat-api.dll" />
<?else ?>
            <CreateFolder />
<?endif ?>
          </Component>
        </Directory>
      </Directory>

      <!-- Per-process shim of the remote kind and of kiosk seats (shim/ workspace). Copied
           here, never to System32; the service installs it only when the operator turns
           isolation on (seat-shim-core). File names stay pulsar-split-* because shim/ and its
           registry keys use them. x64 package: shim\x64\ (+ shimctl) and shim\x86\. ARM64
           package: shim\arm64\ (native module with the Detours backend, the launcher the
           service calls, shimctl), shim\x64\ for x64 apps under emulation and shim\x86\. -->
      <Directory Id="PulsarSeatShimDir" Name="shim">
<?if $(sys.BUILDARCH) = "arm64" ?>
        <Directory Id="PulsarSeatShimArm64Dir" Name="arm64">
          <Component Id="PulsarSeatShimArm64Component" Guid="{3C0E6B27-8F41-4A5D-9E13-B7A2C64D18F5}" Win64="yes">
            <File Id="PulsarSeatShimArm64Dll" Name="PulsarSplitShim.dll" KeyPath="yes"
                  Source="$(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN)\shim\arm64\PulsarSplitShim.dll" />
            <File Id="PulsarSeatShimArm64LaunchExe" Name="pulsar-split-launch.exe"
                  Source="$(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN)\shim\arm64\pulsar-split-launch.exe" />
            <File Id="PulsarSeatShimArm64ctlExe" Name="pulsar-split-shimctl.exe"
                  Source="$(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN)\shim\arm64\pulsar-split-shimctl.exe" />
          </Component>
        </Directory>
        <Directory Id="PulsarSeatShimX64Dir" Name="x64">
          <!-- x64 apps under emulation; no x64 shimctl here (the ARM64 one serves the PC). -->
          <Component Id="PulsarSeatShimX64EmuComponent" Guid="{A7D25F90-1B6C-4E38-8C4F-2E95D0B7A361}" Win64="yes">
            <File Id="PulsarSeatShimX64Dll" Name="PulsarSplitShim.dll" KeyPath="yes"
                  Source="$(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN)\shim\x64\PulsarSplitShim.dll" />
            <File Id="PulsarSeatShimLaunchExe" Name="pulsar-split-launch.exe"
                  Source="$(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN)\shim\x64\pulsar-split-launch.exe" />
          </Component>
        </Directory>
<?else ?>
        <Directory Id="PulsarSeatShimX64Dir" Name="x64">
          <Component Id="PulsarSeatShimX64Component" Guid="{68094D7D-AAAB-4930-959C-902EF4F36708}" Win64="yes">
            <File Id="PulsarSeatShimX64Dll" Name="PulsarSplitShim.dll" KeyPath="yes"
                  Source="$(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN)\shim\x64\PulsarSplitShim.dll" />
            <File Id="PulsarSeatShimLaunchExe" Name="pulsar-split-launch.exe"
                  Source="$(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN)\shim\x64\pulsar-split-launch.exe" />
            <File Id="PulsarSeatShimctlExe" Name="pulsar-split-shimctl.exe"
                  Source="$(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN)\shim\x64\pulsar-split-shimctl.exe" />
          </Component>
        </Directory>
<?endif ?>
        <Directory Id="PulsarSeatShimX86Dir" Name="x86">
          <Component Id="PulsarSeatShimX86Component" Guid="{4D6EA0C5-94F7-4180-9A30-E765F3167E26}" Win64="yes">
            <File Id="PulsarSeatShimX86Dll" Name="PulsarSplitShim.dll" KeyPath="yes"
                  Source="$(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN)\shim\x86\PulsarSplitShim.dll" />
            <File Id="PulsarSeatShimLaunch32Exe" Name="pulsar-split-launch32.exe"
                  Source="$(env.PULSAR_SEAT_BIN)\shim\x86\pulsar-split-launch32.exe" />
          </Component>
        </Directory>
      </Directory>
    </DirectoryRef>

    <!-- Referenced from tauri-bundle.json in both packages. -->
    <ComponentGroup Id="PulsarSeatShim">
<?if $(sys.BUILDARCH) = "arm64" ?>
      <ComponentRef Id="PulsarSeatShimArm64Component" />
      <ComponentRef Id="PulsarSeatShimX64EmuComponent" />
<?else ?>
      <ComponentRef Id="PulsarSeatShimX64Component" />
<?endif ?>
      <ComponentRef Id="PulsarSeatShimX86Component" />
    </ComponentGroup>

    <!-- ================================================================ custom actions -->
    <!-- Exit codes (seat-compat::setup): 0 ok, 3010 reboot, 2 partial, 4 refused, 1 failed.
         With the msi switch the binary maps 2 and 3010 to 0 (Windows Installer treats
         any non-zero EXE exit code as fatal) and records the reboot / partial state in
         %ProgramData%\Pulsar Seat\logs\setup.log; the manager then shows the reboot
         prompt (ServiceStatus.reboot_pending). 4 (refused) and 1 stay fatal. -->
    <!-- `[PulsarSeatDriversDir].`: a directory property always ends in "\", and `\"` would
         be an escaped quote under the MSVC argv rules (the argument would end in a literal
         quote and the folder would never be found). The trailing "." names the same folder.
         The service also drops one stray trailing quote (win/setup.rs normalize_install_args). -->
    <CustomAction Id="PsSetupInstall" FileKey="PulsarSeatServiceExe"
                  ExeCommand="install --msi &quot;--restore-point=[PSRESTOREPOINT]&quot; &quot;--tweak=[PSTWEAKS]&quot; &quot;--features=[PSWINFEATURES]&quot; &quot;--import-cert=[PSIMPORTCERT]&quot; &quot;--drivers=[PulsarSeatDriversDir].&quot;"
                  Execute="deferred" Impersonate="no" Return="check" />
    <!-- Rollback of PsSetupInstall: if a later action fails (StartServices on the Vital
         service, any later deferred action), Windows Installer rolls the files back;
         this reverts the journal first so no system tweak or driver package outlives
         the product. User data is kept. Runs while the files still exist (rollback
         goes in reverse order and InstallFiles comes earlier). -->
    <CustomAction Id="PsSetupRollback" FileKey="PulsarSeatServiceExe"
                  ExeCommand="uninstall --msi --remove-user-data=0"
                  Execute="rollback" Impersonate="no" Return="ignore" />
    <!-- Uninstall must not block removal: Return="ignore". -->
    <CustomAction Id="PsSetupUninstall" FileKey="PulsarSeatServiceExe"
                  ExeCommand="uninstall --msi --remove-user-data=[REMOVEUSERDATA]"
                  Execute="deferred" Impersonate="no" Return="ignore" />

    <!-- Remote kind (seat-setup, `pulsar-seat-service remote-setup ...`). With the msi switch
         only a real failure is non-zero; partial / reboot go to
         %ProgramData%\Pulsar Seat\logs\remote-setup.log. Arguments are quoted; the launch
         conditions above keep whitespace and escape characters out of the properties. -->
    <CustomAction Id="PsRemoteInstall" FileKey="PulsarSeatServiceExe"
                  ExeCommand="remote-setup install --msi &quot;--drivers=[PULSARDRIVERS]&quot; &quot;--consent=[PULSARCONSENT]&quot;"
                  Execute="deferred" Impersonate="no" Return="check" />
    <CustomAction Id="PsRemoteReconcile" FileKey="PulsarSeatServiceExe"
                  ExeCommand="remote-setup reconcile --msi &quot;--drivers=[PULSARDRIVERS]&quot; &quot;--consent=[PULSARCONSENT]&quot;"
                  Execute="deferred" Impersonate="no" Return="check" />
    <!-- Fresh install without PULSARDRIVERS: no third-party driver (a local-only PC gets no
         virtual display). Repairs and upgrades keep the saved choice (empty value). -->
    <SetProperty Id="PULSARDRIVERS" Value="none" Before="PsRemoteInstall" Sequence="execute">
      <![CDATA[NOT PULSARDRIVERS AND NOT Installed AND NOT WIX_UPGRADE_DETECTED AND NOT (REMOVE ~= "ALL")]]>
    </SetProperty>

    <InstallExecuteSequence>
      <!-- Rollback first (it must be scheduled before the action it undoes). Fresh
           installs only: on a failed upgrade / repair the restored old product still owns
           the journal and its uninstall undoes everything later. -->
      <Custom Action="PsSetupRollback" Before="PsSetupInstall">
        <![CDATA[NOT (REMOVE ~= "ALL") AND NOT Installed AND NOT WIX_UPGRADE_DETECTED]]>
      </Custom>
      <!-- Every install, upgrade and repair (idempotent): before the service starts. -->
      <Custom Action="PsSetupInstall" After="InstallServices">
        <![CDATA[NOT (REMOVE ~= "ALL")]]>
      </Custom>
      <!-- Remote kind after the local install step (the data folder and the Event Log source
           exist then), before the service starts. Install: fresh only; reconcile: always. -->
      <Custom Action="PsRemoteInstall" After="PsSetupInstall">
        <![CDATA[NOT Installed AND NOT WIX_UPGRADE_DETECTED AND NOT (REMOVE ~= "ALL")]]>
      </Custom>
      <Custom Action="PsRemoteReconcile" After="PsRemoteInstall">
        <![CDATA[NOT (REMOVE ~= "ALL")]]>
      </Custom>
      <!-- Real uninstall only (not the old product's removal during a major upgrade):
           after the service is stopped, before its files are removed. The service's
           uninstall replays both journal formats: the remote kind's <package>.jsonl
           (seat-setup) first, then seat-compat's changes.jsonl. -->
      <Custom Action="PsSetupUninstall" After="StopServices">
        <![CDATA[(REMOVE ~= "ALL") AND NOT UPGRADINGPRODUCTCODE]]>
      </Custom>
      <!-- Spec 90 §11 item 1: "reboot needed" must reach the caller as 3010. The deferred EXE
           action cannot set a property, so a build that stages signed driver packages
           (PSHASDRIVERS, defined by the generated PulsarSeatDrivers.wxs) always schedules
           the reboot on install / upgrade / repair. msiexec then returns 3010 with
           /norestart (the update path passes it); without /norestart a /qn run restarts
           the PC at the end (installer/README.md). -->
      <ScheduleReboot After="InstallFinalize">
        <![CDATA[PSHASDRIVERS AND NOT (REMOVE ~= "ALL")]]>
      </ScheduleReboot>
    </InstallExecuteSequence>

    <!-- ================================================================ UI -->
    <UI>
      <!-- Spec 90 §11 item 4: do not stop active seats without asking. Full UI only;
           /qn and /qb stop them silently (documented in installer/README.md). -->
      <Dialog Id="PsStopSeatsDlg" Width="320" Height="130" Title="[ProductName]">
        <Control Id="Text" Type="Text" X="15" Y="15" Width="290" Height="70"
                 Text="!(loc.PsStopSeatsText)" />
        <Control Id="Yes" Type="PushButton" X="160" Y="100" Width="70" Height="18" Default="yes" Text="!(loc.PsButtonContinue)">
          <Publish Event="EndDialog" Value="Return">1</Publish>
        </Control>
        <Control Id="No" Type="PushButton" X="236" Y="100" Width="70" Height="18" Cancel="yes" Text="!(loc.PsButtonCancel)">
          <Publish Event="EndDialog" Value="Exit">1</Publish>
        </Control>
      </Dialog>
      <!-- Non-blocking warning (spec 90 §11 item 4: warn about other multi-seat). -->
      <Dialog Id="PsTermSrvDlg" Width="320" Height="140" Title="[ProductName]">
        <Control Id="Text" Type="Text" X="15" Y="15" Width="290" Height="80"
                 Text="!(loc.PsTermSrvText)" />
        <Control Id="Ok" Type="PushButton" X="160" Y="110" Width="70" Height="18" Default="yes" Text="!(loc.PsButtonContinue)">
          <Publish Event="EndDialog" Value="Return">1</Publish>
        </Control>
        <Control Id="Cancel" Type="PushButton" X="236" Y="110" Width="70" Height="18" Cancel="yes" Text="!(loc.PsButtonCancel)">
          <Publish Event="EndDialog" Value="Exit">1</Publish>
        </Control>
      </Dialog>
      <!-- Spec 90 §1.4 / §11 item 7: restore point and system tweaks are explicit, optional
           choices (default off). Wizard (WixUI_InstallDir, Tauri's template):
           InstallDirDlg -> PsOptionsDlg -> VerifyReadyDlg. The later Publish (higher Order)
           of a NewDialog event wins over the built-in one. -->
      <Dialog Id="PsOptionsDlg" Width="370" Height="270" Title="!(loc.PsSetupTitle)">
        <Control Id="Title" Type="Text" X="15" Y="6" Width="340" Height="15" Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="yes"
                 Text="!(loc.PsOptionsTitle)" />
        <Control Id="Description" Type="Text" X="25" Y="23" Width="330" Height="15" Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="yes"
                 Text="!(loc.PsOptionsDescription)" />
        <Control Id="BannerLine" Type="Line" X="0" Y="44" Width="370" Height="0" />
        <Control Id="RestorePoint" Type="CheckBox" X="20" Y="60" Width="330" Height="18" Property="PSRESTOREPOINT"
                 CheckBoxValue="1" Text="!(loc.PsOptRestorePoint)" />
        <Control Id="FastStartup" Type="CheckBox" X="20" Y="90" Width="330" Height="18" Property="PSUI_FASTSTARTUP"
                 CheckBoxValue="1" Text="!(loc.PsOptFastStartup)">
          <Condition Action="hide"><![CDATA[PSHIBERBOOT = "#0"]]></Condition>
        </Control>
        <Control Id="Sleep" Type="CheckBox" X="20" Y="115" Width="330" Height="18" Property="PSUI_SLEEP"
                 CheckBoxValue="1" Text="!(loc.PsOptSleep)" />
        <Control Id="Dumps" Type="CheckBox" X="20" Y="140" Width="330" Height="18" Property="PSUI_DUMPS"
                 CheckBoxValue="1" Text="!(loc.PsOptDumps)" />
        <Control Id="Note" Type="Text" X="20" Y="175" Width="330" Height="40" NoPrefix="yes"
                 Text="!(loc.PsOptNote)" />
        <Control Id="BottomLine" Type="Line" X="0" Y="234" Width="370" Height="0" />
        <Control Id="Back" Type="PushButton" X="180" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17" Text="!(loc.PsButtonBack)">
          <Publish Event="NewDialog" Value="InstallDirDlg">1</Publish>
        </Control>
        <Control Id="Next" Type="PushButton" X="236" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17" Default="yes" Text="!(loc.PsButtonNext)">
          <!-- Rebuild PSTWEAKS from the boxes ("{}" clears it; the service ignores the
               trailing comma). Fast startup only while it is on. -->
          <Publish Property="PSTWEAKS" Value="{}" Order="1">1</Publish>
          <Publish Property="PSTWEAKS" Value="[PSTWEAKS]fast_startup_off," Order="2"><![CDATA[PSUI_FASTSTARTUP AND PSHIBERBOOT <> "#0"]]></Publish>
          <Publish Property="PSTWEAKS" Value="[PSTWEAKS]sleep_off," Order="3">PSUI_SLEEP</Publish>
          <Publish Property="PSTWEAKS" Value="[PSTWEAKS]small_crash_dumps," Order="4">PSUI_DUMPS</Publish>
          <Publish Event="NewDialog" Value="PsComponentsDlg" Order="5">1</Publish>
        </Control>
        <Control Id="Cancel" Type="PushButton" X="304" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17" Cancel="yes" Text="!(loc.PsButtonCancelSetup)">
          <Publish Event="SpawnDialog" Value="CancelDlg">1</Publish>
        </Control>
      </Dialog>
      <!-- Spec/remote 90 §2.4 / §2.5 (parity 2026-11-17): optional Windows features and the
           publisher certificate, each an unchecked, visible choice. The certificate box is
           shown only when this build ships one (PSHASCERT, generated fragment). -->
      <Dialog Id="PsComponentsDlg" Width="370" Height="270" Title="!(loc.PsSetupTitle)">
        <Control Id="Title" Type="Text" X="15" Y="6" Width="340" Height="15" Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="yes"
                 Text="!(loc.PsComponentsTitle)" />
        <Control Id="Description" Type="Text" X="25" Y="23" Width="330" Height="15" Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="yes"
                 Text="!(loc.PsComponentsDescription)" />
        <Control Id="BannerLine" Type="Line" X="0" Y="44" Width="370" Height="0" />
        <Control Id="Vmp" Type="CheckBox" X="20" Y="55" Width="330" Height="18" Property="PSUI_VMP"
                 CheckBoxValue="1" Text="!(loc.PsOptVmp)" />
        <Control Id="HyperV" Type="CheckBox" X="20" Y="77" Width="330" Height="18" Property="PSUI_HYPERV"
                 CheckBoxValue="1" Text="!(loc.PsOptHyperV)" />
        <Control Id="Sandbox" Type="CheckBox" X="20" Y="99" Width="330" Height="18" Property="PSUI_SANDBOX"
                 CheckBoxValue="1" Text="!(loc.PsOptSandbox)" />
        <Control Id="FeatureNote" Type="Text" X="20" Y="120" Width="330" Height="28" NoPrefix="yes"
                 Text="!(loc.PsComponentsNote)" />
        <Control Id="Cert" Type="CheckBox" X="20" Y="152" Width="330" Height="18" Property="PSIMPORTCERT"
                 CheckBoxValue="1" Text="!(loc.PsOptCert)">
          <Condition Action="hide"><![CDATA[NOT PSHASCERT]]></Condition>
          <Condition Action="show"><![CDATA[PSHASCERT]]></Condition>
        </Control>
        <Control Id="CertWarn" Type="Text" X="20" Y="172" Width="330" Height="56" NoPrefix="yes"
                 Text="!(loc.PsOptCertWarn)">
          <Condition Action="hide"><![CDATA[NOT PSHASCERT]]></Condition>
          <Condition Action="show"><![CDATA[PSHASCERT]]></Condition>
        </Control>
        <Control Id="BottomLine" Type="Line" X="0" Y="234" Width="370" Height="0" />
        <Control Id="Back" Type="PushButton" X="180" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17" Text="!(loc.PsButtonBack)">
          <Publish Event="NewDialog" Value="PsOptionsDlg">1</Publish>
        </Control>
        <Control Id="Next" Type="PushButton" X="236" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17" Default="yes" Text="!(loc.PsButtonNext)">
          <!-- Rebuild PSWINFEATURES from the boxes (the service ignores the trailing comma). -->
          <Publish Property="PSWINFEATURES" Value="{}" Order="1">1</Publish>
          <Publish Property="PSWINFEATURES" Value="[PSWINFEATURES]virtual_machine_platform," Order="2">PSUI_VMP</Publish>
          <Publish Property="PSWINFEATURES" Value="[PSWINFEATURES]hyper_v," Order="3">PSUI_HYPERV</Publish>
          <Publish Property="PSWINFEATURES" Value="[PSWINFEATURES]windows_sandbox," Order="4">PSUI_SANDBOX</Publish>
          <Publish Property="PSIMPORTCERT" Value="{}" Order="5">NOT PSHASCERT</Publish>
          <Publish Event="NewDialog" Value="VerifyReadyDlg" Order="6">1</Publish>
        </Control>
        <Control Id="Cancel" Type="PushButton" X="304" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17" Cancel="yes" Text="!(loc.PsButtonCancelSetup)">
          <Publish Event="SpawnDialog" Value="CancelDlg">1</Publish>
        </Control>
      </Dialog>
      <Publish Dialog="InstallDirDlg" Control="Next" Event="NewDialog" Value="PsOptionsDlg" Order="5"><![CDATA[WIXUI_DONTVALIDATEPATH OR WIXUI_INSTALLDIR_VALID="1"]]></Publish>
      <Publish Dialog="VerifyReadyDlg" Control="Back" Event="NewDialog" Value="PsComponentsDlg" Order="5">NOT Installed</Publish>

      <!-- Spec 90 §11 item 11: removal offers to keep or delete %ProgramData%\Pulsar Seat.
           Full UI only (MaintenanceTypeDlg -> Remove -> PsRemoveDataDlg -> VerifyReadyDlg).
           Removal from Settings runs with reduced UI and keeps the data unless
           REMOVEUSERDATA=1 is given; the update download cache is deleted always. -->
      <Dialog Id="PsRemoveDataDlg" Width="370" Height="270" Title="!(loc.PsSetupTitle)">
        <Control Id="Title" Type="Text" X="15" Y="6" Width="340" Height="15" Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="yes"
                 Text="!(loc.PsRemoveTitle)" />
        <Control Id="Description" Type="Text" X="25" Y="23" Width="330" Height="15" Transparent="yes" NoPrefix="yes"
                 Text="!(loc.PsRemoveDescription)" />
        <Control Id="BannerLine" Type="Line" X="0" Y="44" Width="370" Height="0" />
        <Control Id="Text" Type="Text" X="20" Y="60" Width="330" Height="50" NoPrefix="yes"
                 Text="!(loc.PsRemoveText)" />
        <Control Id="RemoveData" Type="CheckBox" X="20" Y="120" Width="330" Height="18" Property="REMOVEUSERDATA"
                 CheckBoxValue="1" Text="!(loc.PsRemoveData)" />
        <Control Id="BottomLine" Type="Line" X="0" Y="234" Width="370" Height="0" />
        <Control Id="Back" Type="PushButton" X="180" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17" Text="!(loc.PsButtonBack)">
          <Publish Event="NewDialog" Value="MaintenanceTypeDlg">1</Publish>
        </Control>
        <Control Id="Next" Type="PushButton" X="236" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17" Default="yes" Text="!(loc.PsButtonNext)">
          <Publish Event="NewDialog" Value="VerifyReadyDlg">1</Publish>
        </Control>
        <Control Id="Cancel" Type="PushButton" X="304" Y="243" Width="56" Height="17" Cancel="yes" Text="!(loc.PsButtonCancelSetup)">
          <Publish Event="SpawnDialog" Value="CancelDlg">1</Publish>
        </Control>
      </Dialog>
      <Publish Dialog="MaintenanceTypeDlg" Control="RemoveButton" Event="NewDialog" Value="PsRemoveDataDlg" Order="5">1</Publish>
      <Publish Dialog="VerifyReadyDlg" Control="Back" Event="NewDialog" Value="PsRemoveDataDlg" Order="6"><![CDATA[Installed AND NOT PATCH AND WixUI_InstallMode = "Remove"]]></Publish>

      <InstallUISequence>
        <Show Dialog="PsStopSeatsDlg" After="CostFinalize">
          <![CDATA[PSSERVICEPRESENT AND (Installed OR WIX_UPGRADE_DETECTED) AND UILevel >= 5]]>
        </Show>
        <Show Dialog="PsTermSrvDlg" After="PsStopSeatsDlg">
          <![CDATA[NOT Installed AND UILevel >= 5 AND PSTERMSRVDLL AND (PSTERMSRVDLL ~<> "#%SystemRoot%\System32\termsrv.dll") AND (PSTERMSRVDLL ~<> "#%windir%\System32\termsrv.dll")]]>
        </Show>
      </InstallUISequence>
    </UI>
  </Fragment>
</Wix>
